        <div class="row">
            
       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026 Declared by KSEAB">
             <div class="blog-content">
               <div class="blog-body">
                 <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026 Declared: Your Gateway to Next Academic Steps!</h1>

                 <p>The wait is finally over for thousands of students across Karnataka! The Karnataka School Examination and Assessment Board (KSEAB) has officially declared the 1st PUC (Class 11) results for the academic year 2025-26. Students can now access their provisional marks online and take the next crucial step in their educational journey. This comprehensive guide will walk you through everything you need to know, from checking your results to understanding the next steps.</p>

                 <div class="section-title">Key Highlights of Karnataka 1st PUC Results 2026</div>
                 <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                   <p>✅ <strong>Result Declared:</strong> March 30, 2026 (most schools); March 31, 2026 (Dakshina Kannada District).</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Official Websites:</strong> result.proed.in, result.bspucpa.in, and kseab.karnataka.gov.in.</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Credentials Needed:</strong> Registration Number/SATS Number and Date of Birth.</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Exams Held:</strong> February 28 to March 17, 2026.</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Overall Pass Percentage:</strong> 68.45%.</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Provisional Marksheet:</strong> Online results are provisional; original mark sheets from colleges.</p>
                 </div>

                 <p>The KSEAB conducted the 1st PUC examinations from February 28 to March 17, 2026, for all three streams: Science, Commerce, and Arts. The results were rolled out in a phased manner to ensure smooth access, with Dakshina Kannada district receiving their results on March 31, a day after most other schools.</p>

                 <div class="section-title">How to Check Your KSEAB 1st PUC Result 2026</div>
                 <p>Checking your Karnataka 1st PUC results online is a straightforward process. Follow these detailed steps to access your scorecard:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Results Portal</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to one of the designated official websites: result.proed.in, result.bspucpa.in, or kseab.karnataka.gov.in. These are the primary portals where your results have been published.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for a prominent link such as "1st PUC Annual Exam Result 2026" or "Karnataka 1st PUC Results 2026". Click on this link to proceed.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Login Credentials</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">You will be prompted to enter your registration number (or SATS Number/Vmithra Reg No) and your date of birth in the specified format (DD/MM/YYYY). Ensure accuracy to avoid any retrieval issues. Your hall ticket will have the correct registration details.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">4. Submit and View Your Result</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">After entering the required information, click on the "Submit" or "Get Result" button. Your Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026, including subject-wise marks and overall status, will be displayed on the screen.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">5. Download and Print Your Marks Memo</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">It is highly recommended to download the provisional marks memo as a PDF and take a printout for your records. This digital copy will be essential for future reference until you receive your original mark sheet from your institution.</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="highlight-text">
                   <strong>Important Note:</strong> Due to potentially high traffic on the result declaration days, the websites might experience some slowdowns. Please be patient and try refreshing the page or using an alternative official portal if you face difficulties.
                 </div>

                 <div class="section-title">Understanding Your Provisional Marksheet</div>
                 <p>The online marksheet you download is provisional and provides a detailed breakdown of your performance. Here’s what it typically includes:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">Student Details</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Your name, registration number, college name, and other personal information.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">Subject-wise Marks</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Individual scores obtained in each subject.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">Total Score</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">The aggregate marks obtained across all subjects.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">Qualifying Status</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Indication of whether you have passed or failed the examination.</div>
                 </div>
                 <p>Remember that the original mark sheets will be issued by your respective schools or colleges at a later date. The online version serves as an immediate reference for your performance.</p>

                 <div class="section-title">Passing Criteria and Supplementary Examinations</div>
                 <p>To successfully pass the Karnataka 1st PUC examination, students must secure a minimum of 35% marks in each subject.</p>
                 <p>For those who may not have achieved the passing marks in one or more subjects, the KSEAB provides an opportunity to appear for supplementary examinations. These exams are crucial for students to clear their backlog subjects and progress to the next academic year without losing a year.</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">Supplementary Exam Schedule</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">The schedule for the Karnataka 1st PUC Supplementary Exam 2026 has not yet been officially released. However, based on previous academic patterns, these examinations are typically conducted in the months following the main results, often between May and June. Students are advised to regularly check the official KSEAB website for announcements regarding application procedures, dates, and fees.</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="section-title">Official Websites for Karnataka 1st PUC Results 2026</div>
                 <p>Here are the official portals where you can check your results:</p>
                 <table class="table table-bordered">
                   <thead>
                     <tr>
                       <th>Website Address</th>
                       <th>Purpose</th>
                     </tr>
                   </thead>
                   <tbody>
                     <tr>
                       <td>result.proed.in</td>
                       <td>Primary portal for 1st PUC results</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>result.bspucpa.in</td>
                       <td>Alternative official result portal</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>kseab.karnataka.gov.in</td>
                       <td>Official KSEAB website for notifications and results</td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                       <td>karresults.nic.in</td>
                       <td>Another common portal for Karnataka examination results</td>
                     </tr>
                   </tbody>
                 </table>

                 <p>Congratulations to all the students who have successfully cleared their Karnataka 1st PUC examinations! This achievement marks a significant milestone in your academic career. For those who need to appear for supplementary exams, stay focused and prepare diligently. The KSEAB is committed to supporting all students in their pursuit of education.</p>
               </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
